    {
      "type": "code",
      "carry": true,
      "title": "A Book class and a Catalog",
      "prompt": [
        "Replace the tuples with classes. Put both at the bottom of the file.",
        "",
        "**`class Book`**: a constructor `Book(string isbn, string title, string author, int year, int copies)`; get-only properties `Isbn`, `Title`, `Author`, `Year`, `TotalCopies`; `AvailableCopies` with a private setter (starts equal to `TotalCopies`); and `ToString()` overridden to return the list line, which now shows copies on the shelf:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "978-0261103344 | The Hobbit | J.R.R. Tolkien | 1937 | 3/3 in",
        "```",
        "",
        "**`class Catalog`**: private `List<Book>` and `Dictionary<string, Book>` (by ISBN) fields, and",
        "",
        "| Member | Does |",
        "|---|---|",
        "| `bool Add(Book book)` | `false` (and adds nothing) when the ISBN is taken |",
        "| `Book? Find(string isbn)` | the book, or `null` |",
        "| `IReadOnlyList<Book> All` | every book in the order added |",
        "| `List<Book> Search(string text)` | title or author contains the text, ignoring case |",
        "",
        "Use one `Catalog` in the top-level code instead of the list and the set. Every command keeps its output, except that book lines end in `3/3 in` instead of `3 copies`.",
        "",
        "Input:",
